Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0025.
Greedy steps sampled from a vocab-parallel argmax (VLLM_GREEDY_LOCAL_ARGMAX=1, default off). Every step all-gathered the
target's full logits from the TP-sharded lm_head (rows x 129,280 columns, 163-187 us a verify round in the TP=2 profile)
before the sampler or the rejection sampler read them. When every request in the step is greedy and asks for nothing that
reads or edits the logits (no temperature, top-k, top-p, min-p, penalties, logit bias, allowed token ids, min_tokens, bad
words, thinking budget, custom logits processors, logprobs, prompt logprobs, structured output), the target returns the
argmax of each logits row from its vocabulary shards instead (compute_logits_argmax): each rank masks its padding columns,
takes the max and argmax of its own columns and all-gathers one (value, index) pair per row, the reduction of vLLM's
LogitsProcessor.get_top_tokens. The plain sampler's greedy rule, or the rejection sampler's (greedy_verify: the greedy
branch of _rejection_kernel plus the bonus row, on argmax ids), then runs on those ids. Bit-exact by construction: both
stock greedy paths take the first index of each row's maximum over the gathered logits read as fp32 (vocab-block argmaxes
keeping the lower index, then the first block among equal block maxima); the pair reduction compares the same values
(bf16 to fp32 is exact), keeps the first index within a shard and the lower rank, i.e. the lower index, across shards,
and never lets a padding column win. Rows holding NaN are the exception (the stock kernels resolve those by reduction
order; VLLM_COMPUTE_NANS_IN_LOGITS keeps the full path). The switch is a host-side decision per step from state every TP
rank shares, made after the captured forward, so both paths coexist with no graph recaptured. A configuration that reads
the logits elsewhere (LoRA, watermarking, a custom sampler, NaN counting, sampling masks, trace replay, batch-sharded
sampling, adaptive or synthetic verification, probabilistic drafting, the acceptance estimator) keeps the full path. The
(value, index) gather is TensorFold's idea (github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold, Apache-2.0), credited in 0012 for the
drafter; this is our implementation for the target. VLLM_GREEDY_LOCAL_ARGMAX_LOG=N logs every N steps how many took
the fast path (an OpenAI request without a temperature gets the generation-config default, which may not be greedy).
Tests: patches/tests/test_greedy_argmax_reduction.py (plain torch, runs anywhere), patches/tests/test_greedy_local_argmax.py.

